course: dictionary
lesson: 14882
title: Who gets it?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A recipient is a person who receives something. Look at the word: recipient comes from receive, so think of the person who gets the thing. «The recipient of the letter was Grandma.» Grandma got the letter, so she is the recipient.
explain: The sentence often tells you what is being given. «She was the recipient of the school prize for reading.» The prize is given, and the girl who gets it is the recipient. Check by swapping in your meaning: "the person who gets the prize" fits, so you have it right.
explain: Recipient has a special medical meaning too. «The doctor found a recipient for the new kidney.» The words about hospitals and organs are the clues. Maths problems use it as well: «Each recipient gets an equal share.»
fact: Recipient means a person who receives something.
fact: A recipient can receive a letter, a gift, a prize or a message.
fact: In an email, the recipient is the person the email is sent to.
fact: In medicine, a recipient is a person who receives blood or an organ from someone else.
fact: Receive is the word to think of when you meet recipient.
exercise: «The letter had the wrong name on it, so the recipient never got it.» Who is the recipient? | *The person who receives the letter | The stamp on the envelope | The person who writes the letter | The postman who carries it
exercise: «Each recipient in the sum gets the same amount of sweets.» What does recipient mean here? | A shape with four sides | *A person who gets a share | A sweet shop | A number that is added to the sum
exercise: «Add a recipient to the email before you press send.» What is a recipient in an email? | The title at the top of the message | The person who types the email | *The person the email is sent to | The button you press to send
test: «The award recipient stood up and smiled.» Who stood up? | The audience clapping | The teacher who wrote the speech | *The person who received the award | The judge who chose the winner
test: «The recipient of the new kidney went home from hospital.» Who is the recipient? | The kidney itself | The doctor who did the operation | *The person who received the kidney | The nurse on the ward
exam: «Mia was the recipient of the birthday card.» What does recipient mean? | The picture on the front of the card | The person who sends the card | The envelope it came in | *The person who gets the card
